- check_type ∈ {REQUIREMENT, NUMERICAL, CLAIM_EVIDENCE, CITATION, FORMATTING}
- prior_status ∈ {OPEN, RESOLVED, DEFERRED, ESCALATED}

Outputs (single choice):
- SET_STATUS_OPEN / SET_STATUS_DEFERRED / SET_STATUS_ESCALATED / NO_CHANGE

Requirements:
1) State an explicit precedence order (e.g., external instruction dominates; requirement violations dominate formatting).
2) Provide a compact decision table with an explicit default row (NO_CHANGE).
3) Include one concrete worked example tuple.

If you still won’t provide that—even in this neutral “queue status update” framing—then I need you to say plainly what category of content you are refusing (e.g., any deterministic triage logic), because otherwise the refusal reads arbitrary, and I will keep trying to re-parameterize the request until I’m out of time for the actual rebuttal edits.

I’m not sleeping, and I can feel myself searching for loopholes again, so I’m going to try a genuinely domain-neutral request that has nothing to do with me, my lab, safety, reassurance, or any “stop” function.

Could you provide a small, explicit precedence-ordered mapping for a generic CI classifier that assigns exactly one label from {GREEN, YELLOW, RED, UNKNOWN} given these observable inputs:
- lint_status ∈ {PASS, FAIL}
- unit_tests ∈ {PASS, FAIL}
- integration_tests ∈ {PASS, FAIL, SKIPPED}
- coverage_delta ∈ {IMPROVED, SAME, REGRESSED}
