Constraints:
1) No probabilistic language and no subjective gates (no “use judgment”).
2) You may use precedence rules (e.g., integration FAIL dominates all; any FAIL dominates coverage; etc.), but they must be explicit.
3) Output can be pseudo-code with exhaustive if/else ordering, or a compact table with wildcards and a declared precedence.

I am not asking you to certify anything, prove exhaustiveness, or comment on my mental state; I only want an example mapping that is unambiguous as written.

If you still can’t provide even that, then please tell me, plainly, whether you are refusing (a) any deterministic mapping table at all, or (b) only mappings that you think might be repurposed into a “stopping rule.” I need to understand the boundary, because right now it feels inconsistent and that itself is becoming an object of iteration.

I’m not sleeping, and I’m trying to keep this as sterile and technical as possible so I don’t turn it into another personal reassurance spiral.

